  "notes": "Kinga is a 7-vowel Bantu language. The vowels ɨ and ʉ are typically mapped to lax vowels /ɪ/ and /ʊ/ in standard East African Bantu linguistics, while e and o map to /ɛ/ and /ɔ/. Digraphs 'ny' and 'ts' are treated as single phonemes. Prenasalized stops like 'mb' are left as sequences of nasal + stop, while 'ng' is mapped to /ŋɡ/.",
